<section class="sg-sec" id="inspired"><h2>What it inspired</h2><ul class="sg-chain"><li><span class="sg-chain-n">Oh! Let My People Go: The Song of the Contrabands (sheet music, arr. Horace Waters)</span> <span class="sg-chain-y">1862</span><span class="sg-chain-h">arrangement</span></li><li><span class="sg-chain-n">Fisk Jubilee Singers' published version</span> <span class="sg-chain-y">1872</span><span class="sg-chain-h">arrangement</span></li><li><span class="sg-chain-n">Tuskegee Institute Singers (Victor)</span> <span class="sg-chain-y">1914</span><span class="sg-chain-h">recording</span></li><li><span class="sg-chain-n">Paul Robeson</span> <span class="sg-chain-y">1940s</span><span class="sg-chain-h">recording</span></li><li><span class="sg-chain-n">Golden Gate Quartet, Spirituals</span> <span class="sg-chain-y">1957</span><span class="sg-chain-h">recording</span></li><li><span class="sg-chain-n">Louis Armstrong, Louis and the Good Book</span> <span class="sg-chain-y">1958</span><span class="sg-chain-h">recording</span></li><li><span class="sg-chain-n">Robert Shaw Chorale (RCA Victor LM/LSC 2580)</span> <span class="sg-chain-y">1964</span><span class="sg-chain-h">recording</span></li><li><span class="sg-chain-n">The Kelly Family, Live; New World</span> <span class="sg-chain-y">1988; 1990</span><span class="sg-chain-h">recordings</span></li></ul></section>
<section class="sg-sec" id="inspired-by"><h2>What it drew on</h2><ul class="sg-chain"><li><span class="sg-chain-n">Book of Exodus 5:1</span><span class="sg-chain-h">the verse the song draws on</span></li></ul></section>
